Refactored the native libp2p runtime around behaviour-owned state machines, atomic authorization updates, typed authenticated gossip, validated network profiles, domain value objects, bounded diagnostics, and shared canonical wire/transcript utilities without changing protocol semantics. `PeerThread` now owns one cohesive native runtime instead of loose publication, proposal, object-ingress, and sync state; failed canonical-view, signer-window, and authorization publications remain independently retryable.
